where high school players would take  money from people to play honor their  accounts and earn them flawless rewards  and that was just booming as a result of  how toxic and almost insulting trials  was at the time the loot was good but  going flawless damn near impossible  unless you had a discord server full of  friends willing to carry you or a ton of  time to spend on heightening your pvp  skills that's all changed with new  alterations to the trials of osiris and  the season of the lost for several  reasons for starters your trials passage  no longer uses your losses to break the  passage before if you got three losses  at any point you could no longer use the  passage and you were forced to reset  starting back at zero the issue in my  mind was that trials matchmaking back in  the day used your card progress as its  main component so if you had a card with  two wins and zero losses the game would  try to put you up against the team with  the same record reset your card and all  of a sudden it's a blind shot as you  were just as likely to face a brand new  team as one that just went flawless and  started a fresh passage now however even  if you lose 10 times in a row if you  still have a couple of wins on your card  those wins will still be counted you  can't go flawless if you have a loss but  winning rounds and matches will still  earn you rewards so flawless isn't your  goal you still will find an incentive to  play and therefore keep the player pool  nice and plentiful going flawless isn't  the only appeal anymore which is huge  for the game mode if you play the game  casually or if you've just ran into some  bad luck with your trials attempts you  will still be rewarded through a  revamped reputation rank system gone are  the days of playing for hours hoping for  a match win just to earn a measly two  tokens and it used to be once you turn  20 you could go to scene 14 and turn  them in just for a new gun but usually  all that work would just lead to him  giving you a in tomorrow's answer rocket  launcher or something turning your  entire effort into a waste of time now  everyone gives you a rank up similar to  how crucible and gambit rank ups work  achieving the next rank will reward you  with the trials and grams straight up  which you can decrypt into a random drop  if you have some shards and glimmer on  hand you can spend that to focus the  engram into something specific that  you've already unlocked in hopes of  achieving that high stat or god roll  that you've always wanted another cool  change is that your passage doesn't end  once you've gone flawless see there is a  huge incentive now to keep playing on a  flawless card because every game won  after you've gone flawless has a chance  of dropping lighthouse level rewards  that's right higher level players no  longer need to keep resetting their  cards and getting tossed back into the  matchmaking pool on some poor  unsuspecting newcomers now in my case i  made the mistake of turning in my  passage after the first flawless of the  weekend and had to recline but the  moment my second trip to the lighthouse  was complete i kept playing with my team  and we got more adapt lighthouse tier  rewards in like 30 minutes than i had  for the entire six hours leading up to  that final run in the past lower level  teams would just constantly get stomped  on and eventually they'd quit trials  altogether dramatically shifting the  matchmaking pool now even if you go in  and are basically a punching bag for  streamers and pro gamers you still have  a lot of opportunity to obtain some  extremely quality loot of course you  won't be racking in the add-up flawless  weapons as often if at all but  high-level players are also no longer  gatekeeping the loot either the high  barrier of entry to get even a single  reward is no longer a factor if you  can't find a group you can now hop in a  trial solo to mix results depending on  the new skill based matchmaking system  if your goal is flawless you still want  to group for sure because your odds of  success going in solo are dramatically  lower now i'm sure there will be  outliers but the overwhelming sentiment  online is that running trials solo is a  very mixed bag but let's focus on the  fact that it's even a possibility which  is huge and is a huge boon for groups as  it means a larger matchmaking pool  before these changes the flawless loot  that you would receive was kind of  whatever too since once you got your  weapon and emblem there was like this  okay what now type situation a few  seasons ago add-up weapons were  introduced which were supposed to make  the flawless rewards meaningful and  encouraged teams to see their cards all  the way through versus playing up to  whatever loot dropped at the three win  five win or seven win benchmarks and  then just resetting their cards now that  skill based matchmaking is a factor it's  less likely that you're gonna face the  usual streamers or the dudes with the  2500 plus elo rating this weekend a lot  of my friends made it to flawless for  the first time and their overall katie's  were well under 1.0 and that is a good  thing i've seen a lot of folks on  twitter complain about skill-based  matchmaking and they're not the pros or  the average players they're usually the  dudes that made a killing by charging  for recoveries and then just stomping on  weaker players and now they actually  have to work for it they're starting to  quake a little bit some of the pro  players though like giggs on the other  hand know their own skill level and are  confident that having a harder challenge  is totally fine and they're still  excited to see players who used to be on  the outside looking in get their  legitimate shot at making it to the  lighthouse that's why everyone needs to  play trials as soon as they can keep the  game mode filled to the brim with  players and earn some sick rewards while  you're at it the messenger and igneous  hammer are two superb guns for all  around crucible play within the current  meta and they can even drop with the  newer perks that have only just come out  this season which makes the sandbox real  interesting to play around with i know  everyone loves kill clip but that gets  boring we've said for years to bungee  that we don't just want more loot we  want better and more interesting loot  since more loot simply means more  garbage in the vault and having the new  perks roll on the trials weapons while  letting players cough up some extra  materials to focus their drops leads to  less clutter more useful rewards and  better payout now here's the best part  of trials right now without a doubt  battlely the anti-cheat system is doing  what it's advertised to do and it's  looking real nice i'm sure there's some  cheating scum doing their damnedest to  get around destiny 2's anti-cheat but as  of right now i cannot tell you how  relieving it is to get killed and go  damn great snipe instead of having no  choice but to second guess and go  maybe they have wall hacks having games  go down to the wire for one team or  another to win always ends in either the  team going damn fair play that was a  really good game or just emphatic  shouting if you pull off the dub you  have to understand how huge that  sentiment is because not too long ago  getting stomped in trials felt like a  self-fulfilling prophecy you expected to  lose and you just resigned yourself to  it i've spent so much time begging my  friends to join me in trials and  literally no one wanted to do it or they  would go in and just go eh i'm just here  for the weekly bounty cause the game  mode simply wasn't fun that's all  changed now and if you're playing  destiny 2 and always wistfully looked at  the dude rocking the glowing trials  armor in the tower now is your chance to  blaze your own path to the lighthouse  and if going flawless still isn't quite  within reach then is perfectly fine  because now you have every opportunity  and right to still take part and take  home some sweet loot rewards there's a  lot of other popular shooters out there  that are kind of hitting a dip whether  it's from player fatigue or from a  myriad of other reasons like the  incredible amount of cheaters and  warzone but destiny 2's endgame pvp is  in a really nice place right now and  it's only going to get better if you  haven't yet give the game a try you'll  want to be as high of a power level as  possible to access trials but the usual  grind for power is not nearly as  imposing as it used to be and getting up  to speed is faster than ever there's a  whole lot of content in destiny 2 right  now so you'll have something to chew on  for quite a bit as you build your  guardian into a pvp machine make no  mistake the changes made to trials of  osiris are amazing the revamped reward  system is top notch stocking up on  materials actually matters now if you  want to focus your loot drops and the  availability of the mode to solo players  opens up the floodgates to keeping the  player population high a must for an  endgame pinnacle activity that wants to  have enough varied matches there have  been so many uplifting stories on  twitter about people getting their first  flawless and for me personally i made it  to the lighthouse a whopping five times  on pc this weekend compared to only two  times in the last year and i was even  able to help lift several of my friends  who had never made it before and one of  those flawlesses was on a passage of  confidence which for those of you who  know that is ridiculous  dude is that your flawless or what oh  yeah [ __ ] yeah let's go  oh yeah it was without doubt the best  weekend of destiny 2 i had ever played  in my last four years and for someone  with over 2 000 hours in this game  that's saying something  [Music]  you

